+++ b/target/linux/bcm53xx/patches-6.18/398-ARM-dts-BCM5301X-R8000-use-the-flow-accelerator-EXPERIMENTAL.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,74 @@
+From: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
+Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL, UNTESTED] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: Netgear R8000: use the
+ flow accelerator
+
+*** This patch has never been applied, built, flashed, or tested on real
+*** hardware. It is a pattern-matched extrapolation from two patches
+*** (328 and 329 in the same series) that another board (the Linksys
+*** EA6900) already has, reviewed and measured on real hardware. It is
+*** included on this experimental branch only, not on `main`, specifically
+*** so it is never built or flashed without a person deliberately choosing
+*** this branch first. See docs/ctf-fa.md and
+*** docs/experimental-hw-offload-branch.md before using it.
+
+The Netgear R8000 (BCM4709A0) already uses switch port 8 (IMP0, gmac2) as
+its only CPU port and already carries a disabled, fixed-link port 5 -
+exactly the prerequisite layout patch 376 ("use IMP0 port 8 as the CPU
+port") added to 30 other BCM5301X boards that didn't have it yet, and
+exactly the spare-port shape patch 329 turned into the flow accelerator's
+trap port on the EA6900. Apply the same two changes patches 328 and 329
+made there:
+
+- port 8 (the CPU port): add the flow accelerator's own "brcm-prepend"
+  DSA tag, so the accelerator sitting between it and gmac2 is in the
+  path (see bgmac-fa.c, patch 723).
+- port 5 (already disabled and fixed-link, unused on this board): turn
+  it into a second CPU port carrying the same tag, which is where b53
+  redirects the frames the accelerator in front of port 8 cannot handle
+  (TTL 1, TCP FIN/RST - see b53_common.c, patches 726/727).
+
+What is NOT known, and cannot be known without a real R8000:
+
+- Whether the BCM4709A0's switch actually has the flow accelerator
+  silicon block (GMAC3 on the internal bus) at all. If it does not,
+  bgmac_fa_probe() finds no GMAC3 core and this patch is a safe no-op -
+  the CPU port keeps working exactly as it does on `main` today, just
+  with an unused tag definition.
+- Whether, if the block exists, its register layout matches the EA6900
+  (BCM4708) closely enough for bgmac_fa_setmode()'s table-init poll to
+  succeed. If it does not, bgmac_fa_open() returns an error and
+  bgmac_open() aborts before resetting the chip or starting DMA - the
+  Ethernet interface behind this switch fails to come up at all until
+  this patch is reverted or the devicetree change undone. This is the
+  one failure mode that is not harmless, which is exactly why this stays
+  off `main` and off the default-built branch.
+
+Signed-off-by: Myles Liu <lyx981mike@gmail.com>
+---
+ arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-netgear-r8000.dts | 6 +++++-
+ 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-netgear-r8000.dts
++++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4709-netgear-r8000.dts
+@@ -214,7 +214,11 @@
+ 		};
+ 
+ 		port@5 {
+-			status = "disabled";
++			/* takes the flow accelerator's traps, see b53_common.c;
++			 * one tagger per tree, and this port carries the
++			 * regular tag
++			 */
++			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
+ 
+ 			fixed-link {
+ 				speed = <1000>;
+@@ -233,6 +237,8 @@
+ 
+ 		port@8 {
+ 			label = "cpu";
++			/* through the flow accelerator, see bgmac-fa.c */
++			dsa-tag-protocol = "brcm-prepend";
+ 		};
+ 	};
+ };
